WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250 line:10%
 The fact is, the
vaccine push is on.

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.340 line:10%
And if some companies can
sort of push that along,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.340 line:10%
well, they're all in, especially
what's going on at Krispy Kreme

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.230 line:10%
right now, that
instituted a new policy.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.900 line:10%
If you can prove you've taken
at least one dose of a vaccine,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.310 line:10%
they'll give you a free donut.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.600 line:10%
So it seemed like a
perfectly good deal to me.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.670 line:10%
I would just go into one
Krispy Kreme after another,

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:19.470 line:10%
repeatedly.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.780 line:10%
Get thousands of donuts
with the same proof.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:22.680 line:10%
Anyway.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.830 line:10%
What's happening now is the food
police are going after Krispy

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.050 line:10%
Kreme, saying that this
is actually advocating

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.400 line:10%
unhealthy behavior, that if
you eat donuts all the time,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.200 line:10%
you can get fat.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.400 line:10%
As if.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.960 line:10%
Anyway, I want to get
the read on all of this

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.430 line:10%
from a guy who meant to do well.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.340 line:10%
Mike Tattersfield is
the Krispy Kreme CEO.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.610 line:10%
Mike, very good to have you.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.350 line:10%
The food police are
after you, Mike.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.780 line:10%
They don't like what you
seem to be advocating.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.720 line:10%
But I think you did also say
everything in moderation,

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.040 line:10%
right?

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:51.840 line:10%
 We have.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.810 line:10%
I mean, if you think
about last year,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.580 line:10%
we did this thing
called acts of joy.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.490 line:10%
You and I chatted about
this about a year ago,

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.710 line:10%
when we opened up to
the healthcare industry,

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.489 line:10%
and they could get any donut, as
many as they wanted, any time.

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:08.700 line:10%
We gave away 30 million
donuts last year in the US.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.790 line:10%
So you know, when
people make a choice--

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:14.910 line:10%
as America gets a hold of the
pandemic and it's a personal

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.540 line:10%
choice people make--

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.620 line:10%
they look for-- if there's
a treat that they can get,

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.390 line:10%
and we can serve it, it's great.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.310 line:10%
I've been actually in the shops.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.950 line:10%
So I was in Chicago and
Louisville this week.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.250 line:10%
And folks who show
me their CDC card.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.250 line:10%
And I go, you want that donut?

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.020 line:10%
They're like, yes sir.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:31.973 line:10%
And they're really happy.

00:01:31.973 --> 00:01:32.940 line:10%
And it's just a little treat.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.100 line:10%
And it just shows the
generosity of the brand.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.570 line:10%
We are a sweet treat brand.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:37.860 line:10%
We get that.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.970 line:10%
 Yeah.
Yeah.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.470 line:10%
And you know, I see
where you're coming here.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:43.740 line:10%
But you know, like people
are very creative, right?

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.170 line:10%
They can come up with
ways to take advantage

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.780 line:10%
of your good deed here.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.450 line:10%
Do you get a lot of customers
who go from Krispy Kreme

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:55.530 line:10%
to Krispy Kreme, still showing
that proof of a vaccine?

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.470 line:10%
I can't be the only
one doing that?

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.447 line:10%
 You know, we won't
make up our programs

00:02:00.447 --> 00:02:02.280 line:10%
for the folks that are going
to try to beat the system.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.530 line:10%
If that's what they
want to do, that's fine.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:09.300 line:10%
The generosity of the brand
is what we really stand for.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:14.220 line:10%
 Now back to the issue that
obesity is a far bigger issue

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.720 line:10%
in this country--
and this was raised

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.120 line:10%
in the Washington Post today--

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.070 line:10%
and that you should
be aware of that.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:24.120 line:10%
And they're lecturing you
on that because however

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.220 line:10%
threatening you
look at the virus,

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.460 line:10%
obesity kills tens
of thousands more

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.160 line:10%
and that your product
leads to that.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.960 line:10%
You say?

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.050 line:10%
 You know, we're a
prod-- we're a donut.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:40.380 line:10%
And our brand actually serves
it primarily in dozens.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.750 line:10%
We're a sweet treat.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:43.800 line:10%
And it's shared.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.380 line:10%
People mostly use a
Krispy Kreme occasion,

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.670 line:10%
and they share it
with their friends.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.330 line:10%
And the average American visits
a Krispy Kreme about four times

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.390 line:10%
a year.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:55.410 line:10%
So I think we're OK there-- in
moderation, like anything else.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:58.770 line:10%
People will always
want a sweet treat.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:02.160 line:10%
They'll make their own judgment.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.060 line:10%
 No, I think you're
right about that.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.000 line:10%
I just wanted to get
your take on all of that

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.420 line:10%
because no good deed
goes unpunished.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:10.320 line:10%
People can push it.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.720 line:10%
But I'm going to warn Americans
that you really shouldn't

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.400 line:10%
do what I've been doing
and go from Krispy Kreme

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.320 line:10%
to Krispy Kreme,
because that's just--

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.440 line:10%
 You know, I'll be at the
shops, so maybe I'll find you.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.260 line:10%
I mean, I can tell you that
when I dropped off some donuts

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.050 line:10%
at the vaccination
centers this week as well,

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.390 line:10%
they just love it.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:27.190 line:10%
They're working hard.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:31.040 line:10%
So the least we could do
is just help them out.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.380 line:10%
 Well, I'm getting word
because a lot of your stores

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.880 line:10%
have photos of me saying,
had you seen this man?

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.150 line:10%
And so we'll see what happens.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.450 line:10%
 Have you gotten to
our flagship shop?

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.317 line:10%
 Mike Tattersfield of K--

00:03:40.317 --> 00:03:41.120 line:10%
yeah--

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.260 line:10%
 Have you made it
to the flagship--

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.070 line:10%
 --to Krispy Kreme--

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.070 line:10%
 --shop in New York?

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:44.870 line:10%
 No.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.270 line:10%
No, I haven't been
to the flagship shop.

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.360 line:10%
But any way you can get
me there, I'm there.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.160 line:10%
So Mike--

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:49.960 line:10%
 You [INAUDIBLE].

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.590 line:10%
 --thank you very, very much.

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:55.030 line:10%
All right, thank you
very much on this.

